  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Nature and Mechanism
    
    Drift-coalesce (glacial) is an aurora-derived ability in which crystallization occurs *inward* before manifesting outward — ice forming first in the practitioner's own body. Marrow hardens into lattice-work. Capillaries freeze solid. Breath becomes visible, then dangerous, each exhalation depositing frost-flowers that will not melt. The process, once initiated, does not fully reverse. Practitioners who learn to redirect the coalescence outward — into weapons, barriers, or the bodies of others — retain permanent markers: blackened and cracked flipper-tips, eyes clouded with aurora-shimmer, a radiating cold severe enough that even their shadow frosts the ground beneath it.
    
    The term 'mastered' appears frequently in secondary literature. It should be understood as relative. No practitioner has demonstrated full control. The ability demands its price in frostbite that never heals — what adherents of the Mandatum∴absconditu, the Nightshelf doctrine of strategic secrecy, call the cost of *marrow and breath*.
    
    ## Discovery
    
    The earliest documented encounter is attributed to Lovumruius~ Domina, an Aurora-affiliated practitioner, at the Veil Vents — a cluster of geothermal vents ringing the Still Pools — during the Faction Wars. Accounts describe the ability as having emerged "wild" when the Aurora Berg's boundaries destabilized and deeper energies surfaced through breach-points that should have remained sealed. The coalescence was not developed; it was stumbled into. ☽'Netemia Glow-bringer is the first practitioner recorded to have survived sustained exposure and achieved weaponized redirection. Her predecessors did not survive.
    
    ## Applications and Governance
    
    Beyond combat, drift-coalesce carves navigable passages through deep ice. These glacial passages have become controlled trade routes governed under Nightshelf pacts. Their diversion to unauthorized buyers constitutes a killing offense — a prohibition enforced with sufficient seriousness that the Cell's wanted notice for Glow-Trader Vaulius-Phantasm~ and Void-Merchant Valveus-morb~ specifically charges passage-diversion alongside unauthorized aurora-crystal extraction.
    
    The ability manifests across numerous locations: Light Ingjeizhi, the Glow-Fissure, Promenade Hei, Terrace Momiou, the Beacon Stack, and others — a geographic spread that suggests the underlying phenomenon is not localized but follows the Berg's corruption network.
    
    ## Cultural Legacy
    
    The Nightshelf cautionary proverb *'Don't coalesce what you can't shed'* originated as practical warning about uncontrolled crystallization. Its application has since broadened to encompass alliances, debts, and obligations that take root where they cannot be removed. Mandatum∴absconditu adherents regard the glacial coalescence as a sacred *mark of sight*, honoring the permanent frostbite as divine rather than cursed.
